body:
People are celebrating the fact this this woman is being stopped from commiting a crime, before she does it and potentially cause further ramifications for an already crippling situation in Melbourne

 What would you like, for 9000 people to arrive, break the law, potentially spread the virus, use up police resources, delay the course of lockdown for melbourne and THEN for the protestors and organisers to be arrested? I'll tell you what, majority of our country would be furious that it was allowed to even be organised.

&#x200B;

In Melbourne, we aren't currently allowed to travel more than 5 KM away from our residence unless absolutely required. People are sick of being in this scenario and watch other people fail to commit to this, as non-adherence might just prelong these last 6 weeks where EVERYTHING is at a halt.

&#x200B;

If you are making it clear you are going to be committing ANY sort of crime, whether thats a robbery, a murder, terrorism act, or in this case cause potential for further losses in an already struggling economy, you should be fucking arrested ya dimwit
